{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"contained-blue-nandine","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\n`make worktree name=<branch>` fails immediately for every invocation:\n\n```\n/bin/sh: branch: No such file or directory\nmake: *** [worktree] Error 1\n```\n\nNo worktree is created. The documented one-command path for provisioning a worktree is\ntherefore unusable, and `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` both direct agents and\ncontributors to it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn the `worktree` target, the recipe line\n\n```\n\t@set -e; \\\n```\n\nends with a backslash continuation, but the lines that follow it are `@#`-prefixed\ncomment lines:\n\n```\n\t@set -e; \\\n\t@# Default is ~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>, NOT a sibling of the checkout.\n```\n\n`@#` is a make recipe-prefix plus `#`, which make strips only at the start of a recipe\nline — it is not a make comment when the previous line continues into it. So the two\nlines are joined and handed to the shell as a single command:\n\n```\nset -e; @# Default is ~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>, NOT a sibling of the checkout.\n```\n\n`#` does not begin a shell comment mid-word, so the shell parses the text as a command\nand reads `<branch>` as an **input redirection** from a file named `branch`. That file\ndoes not exist, producing `/bin/sh: branch: No such file or directory`.\n\nThe first comment line also has no trailing backslash, so the recipe line terminates\nthere and the entire remaining body — the `target_dir=` default, the fetch, the\n`git worktree add`, and the venv provisioning — never runs as part of that line.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThe target's own comment block documents a sandbox-safety fix (worktrees must not\ndefault to a sibling of the checkout). That fix is unreachable because the comment\ndocumenting it is what breaks the target.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `make worktree name=<branch> dir=<path>` creates a worktree at `<path>` branched\n      from a freshly-fetched `origin/main` and provisions its `.venv`, verified by\n      running it and showing the resulting `git worktree list` entry and a working\n      `.venv/bin/python`.\n- [ ] The explanatory comments are preserved, relocated so they are real make comments\n      rather than shell text, verified by the diff.\n- [ ] A test asserts the target's recipe contains no `@#` sequence on a line that is a\n      continuation of a previous line, so this class of defect cannot return; the test\n      fails against the current Makefile before the fix.\n- [ ] `make worktree` with no `name=` still prints its usage message and exits 2,\n      verified by the command's output and exit status.","id":"8c79-5cf4-0773-4afc","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree is broken: @# comment inside a continued recipe line makes the shell parse <branch> as a redirect"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789758889673546462,"uuid":"4f19e0f2-615f-4ba2-b2dd-991f82ef7fb0"}